{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014roqTY6bnsRGKejjJkX71C","type":"tool_result","content":"=== INTENT ===\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: delivery-intent\nid: DI-RATE-LIMIT\ntitle: Enforce organization-level request limits with visible decisions\nclaim: proposed\nsource:\n  uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n  captured_at: '2026-08-02T00:00:00Z'\n  sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\nsuccess:\n- A versioned policy schema rejects invalid limits and windows.\n- Resolution produces exactly one effective policy for an organization.\n- Request 101 is denied after 100 allowed requests in the same window.\n- The denial returns a stable reason and emits matching decision telemetry.\nout_of_scope:\n- Replacing provider-owned usage metering.\n- Choosing production storage or deployment infrastructure.\n---\n# Enforce organization-level request limits with visible decisions\n\n## Delivery outcome\n\nFor every organization request, resolve one effective rate-limit policy, deny request 101 when the effective limit is 100, and expose a stable reason plus decision telemetry without changing provider-owned metering.\n\n## Evidence boundary\n\nThis artifact records a **proposed** claim. Its source, capture time,\nand content hash are recorded in frontmatter; the claim is not implementation\nevidence by itself.\n=== STEEL THREAD ===\n# Steel Thread\n\n1. [`LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID`](legs/LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID.md)\n2. [`LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED`](legs/LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED.md)\n3. [`LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED`](legs/LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED.md)\n4. [`LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE`](legs/LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE.md)\n\nThis is a derived critical capability path. It records ordering, not\nimplementation completion or dispatch authority.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14a2f32c-9fea-4795-8643-1c0e730b4775","uuid":"61055e86-fa76-4e0a-a0e1-1aaa44dfe0d7","timestamp":"2026-09-14T22:08:58.436Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== INTENT ===\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: delivery-intent\nid: DI-RATE-LIMIT\ntitle: Enforce organization-level request limits with visible decisions\nclaim: proposed\nsource:\n  uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n  captured_at: '2026-08-02T00:00:00Z'\n  sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\nsuccess:\n- A versioned policy schema rejects invalid limits and windows.\n- Resolution produces exactly one effective policy for an organization.\n- Request 101 is denied after 100 allowed requests in the same window.\n- The denial returns a stable reason and emits matching decision telemetry.\nout_of_scope:\n- Replacing provider-owned usage metering.\n- Choosing production storage or deployment infrastructure.\n---\n# Enforce organization-level request limits with visible decisions\n\n## Delivery outcome\n\nFor every organization request, resolve one effective rate-limit policy, deny request 101 when the effective limit is 100, and expose a stable reason plus decision telemetry without changing provider-owned metering.\n\n## Evidence boundary\n\nThis artifact records a **proposed** claim. Its source, capture time,\nand content hash are recorded in frontmatter; the claim is not implementation\nevidence by itself.\n=== STEEL THREAD ===\n# Steel Thread\n\n1. [`LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID`](legs/LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID.md)\n2. [`LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED`](legs/LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED.md)\n3. [`LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED`](legs/LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED.md)\n4. [`LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE`](legs/LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE.md)\n\nThis is a derived critical capability path. It records ordering, not\nimplementation completion or dispatch authority.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
